WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.820
When integration came up, then it made things a little bit different.

2
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.180
When I was at Westlake High, I took a geography [?] class.

3
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.800
Mrs. [Meyers?] was the teacher.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:19.720
And I was the only black in that class.

5
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:25.840
I went down to [Danny Cupid’s?] office because he was the counselor.

6
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.460
I told him I wanted out.

7
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.860
I wanted out of the class.

8
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.520
He said, "Why?"

9
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.680
I said, "Just too uncomfortable in the class."

10
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.400
Too uncomfortable in the class being the only black in the class.

11
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.820
I felt so uncomfortable in the class.

12
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.360
It wasn't the information.

13
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:51.360
It wasn't the class itself.

14
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.720
It was the people.

15
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.380
I said, "Man, take me out put me in business math."

16
00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:58.920
He said, "Okay.

17
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.820
I’m going to take you out."

18
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.520
He took me out put me in business math.

19
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.320
Coming down the hall, Mrs. [Meyers?] called for me.

20
00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.380
She said, "I need to see you in my classroom.

21
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.860
I want to talk to you."

22
00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:18.760
She said, "I am very troubled that you dropped my class.

23
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.720
Was any of the kids in here causing you any problems?"

24
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.560
I said, "Not directly."

25
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:35.840
She says, "Was it me that caused you to drop my class?"

26
00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.220
I said, "Not directly."

27
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.400
She pulled a book out.

28
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:47.280
She said, "You made straight A's and B's in this class, so why did you drop this class?

29
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.000
She said, "What's the problem?

30
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:49.900
What was the problem?"

31
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:57.120
I said, "Look, when blacks come to white schools . . . Whites don't come to black schools.

32
00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:04.600
When blacks come to white schools, whites have the general conception that we're all stupid and dumb.

33
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:05.660
Okay?

34
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.480
They feel black people are dumb, stupid, and slow.

35
00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:18.140
So they are very sensitive that, “Don't ask him a question because if he don't know the answer, it's going to be so shameful.

36
00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.460
Don't ask him.

37
00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.620
It's going to be so shameful.”

38
00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:25.120
Everybody feels on edge.

39
00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:34.120
Now so when the teacher asks the white kids, the white kids, oh, they’re uncomfortable to answer the question because if they don't know it,

40
00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.940
oh, they don’t want the black kid in there to know they don't know.

41
00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.920
So they become what?

42
00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.320
Very uncomfortable.

43
00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:50.180
Okay, so the bottom line what I found out in her class . . . And I told her that I found out,

44
00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.800
that look, we're all human beings.

45
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:59.920
White folks are no smarter than black folks and black folks are no smarter than white folks, or dumber.

46
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:07.960
But for some superiority here, people feel threatened by each other.

47
00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.260
We can't just live.

48
00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.420
We got to be inferior.
